@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

<section class="intro">
    <h2>Live U.S. nuclear outage data, end to end</h2>
    <p>
        This app pulls real outage and generation data from the
        <a href="https://www.eia.gov/opendata/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EIA (U.S. Energy Information Administration) API</a>
        on a recurring schedule, persists it in Postgres, and exposes it three ways: a browsable
        dashboard, a JSON REST API, and an MCP server for AI clients. Register an account to
        follow specific facilities and see a filtered view of just the ones you care about.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="features">
    <h3>What's actually running under the hood</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Scheduled background ingestion from the EIA API, with idempotent upsert so re-fetching never creates duplicates</li>
        <li>JWT authentication (HttpOnly cookie) with per-user facility watchlists</li>
        <li>A JSON REST API at <span class="mono">/api/outages</span> &mdash; CRUD, facility/date filters, and trend aggregation</li>
        <li>A bounded, single-purpose AI feature that turns a date range of outage rows into a plain-English summary</li>
        <li>An MCP server exposing outage data as tools for AI clients like Claude Desktop</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="quick-links">
    <h3>Get started</h3>
    <div class="link-grid">
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Read" class="btn btn-primary">View outages</a>
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="DataVisualization" class="btn">Explore charts + AI summary</a>
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="About" class="btn">About this project</a>
    </div>
</section>
